<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 10 trln rbls in bills on Dec 25.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 10 trln rbls in bills on Dec 25.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will auction 7.5 trillion roubles in six-month GKO discount Treasury bills (series 22064) and 2.5 trillion roubles in a new tranche of OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24004) on December 25, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auctions follow:  </p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number			 22064</p>
<p>    Issue volume			  7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			 1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor				   210 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			 July 23, 1997</p>
<p>Full details of the bond auction:</p>
<p>    Series number			 24004</p>
<p>    Issue volume			  2.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			 1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)		   154 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			 May 28, 1997</p>
<p>    Next coupon date		    Feb 26, 1997</p>
<p>    Coupon rate			   40.05 pct</p>
<p>    Original issue date		 Nov 22, 1995</p>
<p>In money terms the coupon amounts to 99,851 roubles, less accruals of 30,723.38 roubles.</p>
<p>On December 25 the finance ministry will repay about 6.07 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of six-month T-bills (series 22037).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
